# Shell scripts are sourced by bash (Git Bash on Windows, Cygwin on the CI
# agent), which treats a trailing CR as part of the command itself — a checkout
# with CRLF fails at the first line with `$'\r': command not found`.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system gitconfig, so a fresh
# clone converts these to CRLF on every Windows machine unless told otherwise.
# eol=lf overrides that per-path, independent of any user or system setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
